# [O-29] pcrec-bench 2026-09-16: the `ext`/AUX CONTROL. This shape
# (an `ext` subtree as the last content of a block, immediately followed
# by a blank line, a comment line, or end of file) does NOT share O-29's
# drop, and this fixture is the artifact-backed reason why, not just the
# claim: `#section aux` rows are pushed PER LINE as each is read
# (`aux_push`, at the moment the opener or a deeper line is dispatched),
# never deferred to `RXT_CLOSE_FRAME`/`close_section_frame` — and that
# macro is ALSO a no-op for a tree frame regardless (`if (!(F)->tree)`
# guards both the constraint check and the section push), so the old
# buggy `ndepth = 1` reset and the fixed closing loop behave IDENTICALLY
# here: neither one had, or has, anything to do when a tree frame closes.
# Same three closing sites as the provenance/variant fixtures, purely for
# symmetry — none of the three is special for `ext`.
pattern p1 a
ext bench
  note aux content under block 1

pattern p2 b
ext bench
  note aux content under block 2
# a comment, not a blank line, separates block 2 from block 3
pattern p3 c
ext bench
  note aux content under block 3
